    {
      "id": "p0206-b006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "To preserve this scene's logic, the translator localized \"Yell\" as ki iroi koe o ageru, which literally means \"to let out a yellow voice\" but functionally means \"to cry out in a shrill voice\". The translator then localized \"Yellow\" as ki iroi botan (\"yellow button\"). So although it uses slightly different wording, the Japanese scene closely parallels the English script in tone and intent.",
        "raw": "To preserve this scene's logic, the translator localized \"Yell\" as ki iroi koe o\nageru, which literally means \"to let out a yellow voice\" but functionally means\n\"to cry out in a shrill voice\". The translator then localized \"Yellow\" as ki iroi\nbotan (\"yellow button\"). So although it uses slightly different wording, the\nJapanese scene closely parallels the English script in tone and intent.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.2874395,
          0.45613571,
          0.89208509,
          0.54207143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28541042,
          0.45542143,
          0.90315372,
          0.54314286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          47,
          49,
          50,
          51,
          52
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "为了保住场景逻辑，译者把“Yell”译成 ki iroi koe o ageru，字面是“发出黄色的声音”，实际指“尖声喊叫”；再把“Yellow”译成 ki iroi botan（黄色按钮）。虽然措辞略有变化，日版的语气和用意却与英文十分接近。",
        "status": "draft",
